Unfortunately it sounds like the ‘Open Box’ radios on offer are customer returns that have not been tested, especially if they have the previous users codeplug still in them.  Radioddity are just a reseller so they probably don’t have any way of testing or resetting returned items. <br><br>One of the reasons for the previous user returning them would be that they would not enter firmware update mode. That is a known problem when doing factory resets on certain firmware versions. <br><br>The only way they can be fixed would be to open them up and reflash the bootloader using an external debugger and Roger’s instructions. <br><br>Or just keep requesting a replacement until a good one arrives. <br><br>Colin.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Sat Apr 16, 2022 9:53 am</p><hr />
